      "text": "5:40 São Paulo, Brazil \nThank you for this fascinating video! 🇧🇲\n\nI must confess that I spent years imagining Bermuda as a desolate, mysterious place where a strange magnetic triangle swallowed planes into the ocean. 😂 Now I discover an island with an extraordinary history, an ingenious way of dealing with its lack of fresh water, and a surprisingly important role in the global economy.\n\nI'm currently developing a dystopian story that explores unusual places and the strange possibilities hidden within them. Your video has given me a new perspective on Bermuda. I'm already wondering what my characters might discover on an island where water is precious and wealth comes from managing the world's risks. 🤔\n\nSome places become even more fascinating when reality turns out to be stranger than fantasy.\n\nThank you for the inspiration!",
      "likeCount": 0,
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T04:47:52Z",
      "replyCount": 0,
      "replies": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Ugx8Yx963cbpq_XBT9J4AaABAg",
      "author": "@worldlifejournal",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/A_pUZ2JQXKH2IC0sS99qo1gbq_7J-7T_vi2uJ9-oYgphMXxY4FHLUij3wRA96k2_emqz5ApW8g=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "The 'island paradox' framing is spot-on — 60,000 people thriving on a rock with no rivers and virtually zero natural resources. What fascinated me most is how Bermuda turned geographic isolation into an advantage, building wealth on finance and tourism while importing almost everything. A powerful reminder that resources matter less than how a community organizes itself.",
